A||N||17||Formula88||Wheel Alignment Shops?||||5||
Z||000000||Formula88||05-24-2001||12:29 PM||||Can anyone recommend a good wheel alignment shop in N.C.?  I'd prefer the Triangle area, but I'll travel up to 200 miles, just to make sure it's done right.  BTW, it's for my 88 Formula.||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||05-24-2001||07:33 PM||||chk with Hooper or FieroLisa, there from Greensboro I think. She had hers done after the lowering job.||||reg||1
Z||000002||PBJ||05-24-2001||07:46 PM||||You should be able to ask for print outs of before and after. If you don't know what the numbers mean than post 'em and we will help.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GTPete.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||KissMySSFiero||05-24-2001||08:02 PM||||IM sorry buti dont see whats so difficult for these allignment shops on doing a fiero right.  Ive done  my own when i worked at a shop.  it was very simple.  i have a formula.  the only hard part was breaking the strut bolt loose.  i have to get a lot of stuff done to my car before i get it done again(i no longer work on cars so i have to pay...ugh)  but if they give me hassle im goin out to their shop and doin it my damn self.  ive never really seen the susp. on pre88 cars but from the books ive seen its simpler.  i think people are just afraid of fieros because the engine's in the back.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000004||RobertVol||05-24-2001||08:21 PM||||It has been my experience that its not the "name" of the shop you go to. Its the people working under the roof of the shop. I have been to Big name shops and little name local shops and it always comes down to who does the work in the shop. I will say this.. once you find one you can trust ...Hold on to them <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Good luck finding one ! ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||05-24-2001||11:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KissMySSFiero:<BR><B>i think people are just afraid of fieros because the engine's in the back.  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's the problem.  Fear and ignorance.  I want a shop intelligent to know the 88's have a different susupension and that it has to have a 4 wheel alignment.  ANY shop can do it, if they have their head out of their a$$.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||05-24-2001||11:30 PM||||I've been taking my Fieros to one of the local Pontiac dealers(Jalk Walker for locals), and have nothing but praise for their work. It does depend on the knowledge of the staff, but I also get a sense of security knowing the guys working on my Fieros have the factory books and computers to answer any questions they have. The local dealer charges $50 for a 4 wheel alignment. They get everything right(even the steering wheel is straight), and they don't crush my coolant tubes(a major fear of mine). Plus, $50 isn't much more if any from waht a local garage would charge, I've never looked into having a garage do the work.<P>I would suggest having Pontiac take a stab at it.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Eric||05-24-2001||11:43 PM||||Don't get me started...  They didn't torque my suspension bolts last time.  They even left a 1/2 inch of slop on the lower strut to spindle bolt.  You know that one that should be torqued to 140 ft/lbs.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Formula88||05-24-2001||11:46 PM||||Which is why I want recommendatoins from people who have gotten their Fiero aligned (preferably an 88) and are happy with the work.  I want to avoid that kind of stuff, if at all possible.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Bob Englert||05-25-2001||08:03 AM||||John:<P>I had great luck with Piedmont Truck Tire here in Greensboro.  They knew exactly what to do with the car, and they got the caster right on my blue GT that the first shop screwed up completely.  <P>I was very frustrated with the car after the first alignment.  The the first shop, (a local Goodyear dealer) did not tell me the right front caster was way out of spec, and the car drove TERRIBLE.  After taking it to Piedmont Truck Tire, and explained what I was experiencing, the car was great.  They gave me the printout, and all the values were within specs.  They told me to bring it back if it didn't feel right.<P>After driving it around for about 1 hour I called the shop back to thank them.  The maroon GT will be going to see them as soon as the front end rebuild is finished.<P>Highly recommended!  If you come over to have it aligned let me know and we can get together for lunch.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroHarry||05-25-2001||08:10 AM||||I took mine to Fire#$%^&* once and it will never go back again.<BR>This clown told me every Fiero pulls to the left that it an inherant trait, I just grumbled and left. Sure as ****  after he got done it pulled to the left!<BR>Oh well nuff said about them......<P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>1985 GT 264K+ <I>"TEMPTATION"</I><BR><B>"Im not driving to fast, Im flying to low!"</B>||||reg||8
Z||000011||KissMySSFiero||05-25-2001||08:20 AM||||Ive heard horrow storys of shops changing tire pressusre to get the car to drive straight.  you should always ask for a before and after printout.  that way you can see if they just "Set the toe, and let it Go" or actually did an alignment.  also watch them.  First you must get a 4wheel alignment.  they MUST do the rear first.  if they dont then they dont know what theyre doin or possible its within specs. but ask.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000012||Formula88||05-25-2001||09:56 AM||||Thanks for the tips, people.  Looks like I'll be calling Piedmont Truck Tire for an appointment.  <P>Yeah, and shop that tells me "they all do that" is obviously staffed with morons.  I've run into that type of thing before - and that's what I'm hoping to avoid here.<P>Hope everyone has a Fiero-licious holiday weekend!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000013||FieroLisa||05-25-2001||12:54 PM||||NO ONE in greensboro wanted to do my freakin car!!! Finally the Merchants thats right near my place (umm I dont know the intersection, but its like right near the KMart and Target on Bridford) did it...they gave me a readout, and were real nice about it.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Formula88||05-25-2001||02:45 PM||||Makes you wonder, don't it?  It's like they're afraid to work on a Fiero cuz it's this weird exotic car.  Ok, I think they're pretty exotic, but the hardware is regular GM stuff.  Even the '88's aren't designed like some never before seen racecar.  Thanks for the tip, Lisa!  Are you actually gonna be able to make some of the NC Fiero meetings this summer?  As soon as I started showing up, you disappeared.  Did Pat warn you about me, or what?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||6
