Z||000016||KissMySSFiero||05-25-2001||04:32 PM||||The thing i dont understand about some techs is that the adjustments arent that much different than many other cars.  and even if they were.  if they have hunter machines, which are the top of the line,  then you can go into the program and it literally tells you everything you need to know to make the adjustments.  its kinda like vanna white just touching the letters on wheel of fortune instead of turning them.  How can it get any simpler.     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000017||rogergarrison||05-25-2001||08:14 PM||||most of the time the pulling to one side is caused by caster out of spec. The only way to correct it without using new slotted ball joints is to remove the upper a arm cross shaft and move the shims around. Most guys dont know that or are to lazy to do that much work. They just set toe and tell ya thats the best it will go, get your money and send you on your way.<P>Im with Eric on that, my car will NEVER-EVER SEE THE INSIDE OF ANOTHER DEALERSHIP unless somebody buys it from me first.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 05-25-2001).]||||reg||1
